# Story 92: Sharing Groups, Lanes & Tabs (45s)
# Hook: Share one pane, or a whole tab. Each level brings its children along.
# Duration: 45s
# Source: story-092-sharing-groups-lanes-tabs.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 7

[00:00.0 --> 00:03.0]
Share one pane, or a whole tab. Each level brings its children along.

[00:03.0 --> 00:10.0]
Start rysh and split a couple of panes so we have a group, a lane, and a tab worth sharing.

[00:10.0 --> 00:16.0]
Double-Escape into rysh mode. The share command works at four scopes: pane, panegroup, lane, and tab.

[00:16.0 --> 00:24.0]
##share panegroup control shares the active group -- every stacked pane inside it comes along.

[00:24.0 --> 00:31.0]
##share lane shares the whole column: all groups, all panes in that lane, as one unit.

[00:31.0 --> 00:39.0]
And ##share tab publishes the entire tab -- every lane and pane your collaborators need, in one command.

[00:39.0 --> 00:45.0]
##share list shows all of them together. Share at the level that fits the work.

